==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 7.33 seconds<sup>220f</sup>, delay 20~22 seconds<sup>600f~660f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~22 seconds<sup>600f~660f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The Kory is a major threat. Basically, if it was only Kory you could just spam long-rangers. However, if you do that, Bun Bun Black will just kill them quickly. So you will need to use meatshields, two is recommended. The rest should be filled with long rangers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]].

Don't bring any units if their durability is lower than 2,800 (5,600 for a close ranger) because 2,800 is the damage of Kory's waves. Bring at least one [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]]/[[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] cat for Bun Bun Black, though not [[Knockback|knockback]], [[Slow|slow]], or [[Freeze|freeze]]. While they can stall Bun Bun Black for a few moments, Kory will be able to attack much more easily. Once Bun Bun Black is knocked back, this is a golden opportunity for you to attack Kory (Bun Bun Black is knockbacked every 77,777 health).

You can avoid Kory's waves by using weak meatshields so that when they're killed by Bun Bun Black, Kory will miss, and the wave attack won't form. For example, [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] withstands a Bun Bun Black hit, being victim to Kory's waves, while his Evolved Form will die more easily from Bun Bun Black's attacks, making Kory miss his target. If you have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], you pretty much win as long as you shield him from the Doge Darks. He has high health so he can take various hits from Kory while also blocking his waves and saving your backline, takes 1/4 damage from [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] (1/5 with treasures, which could become a whopping 1/10 if he [[Weaken|weakens]] Bun Bun Black), effectively stalling Bun Bun Black. With Octo, all you need is to send constant meatshielding, ensure you have money to keep sending out Octopus Cats and to stack attackers.

For 4-crown difficulty, this can be quite difficult as Bun Bun Black and Kory will pretty much destroy your units with the 3.0 magnification. It is suggested to use the double research combo ([[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Skelecat]], [[Mr. (Special Cat)|Mr.]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer]]), along with [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameramen]] and Paris stacking. Also, you could stack Necro-Dancers along with Cameramen, and do perfect timing with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to kill Kory and Bun Bun Black. Awakened Bahamut should be deployed just right before they sync in position.

